{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["And Elohim called the rakia 'shamayim' — as I explained above, that is to say: it is called שמים everywhere in the Torah. And the upper heavens were included in 'שמי השמים וכל צבאם', and ״הן לה׳ אלהיך השמים ושמי השמים״ וגו׳." "And it was evening and it was morning, a second day — the day had inclined toward evening, and afterward ״ויהי בקר״ of a second day. Thus the second day of the six days that the Holy One, blessed be He, spoke of in the Ten Commandments was completed, and now the third day began in the morning."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T23:16:47.869189426Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}